  "pr": {
    "description": "### Overview\\nFixes the recurring webhook dispatch failures from OPS-77. On-call should\\nstop seeing the repeated dispatch pages after this lands.\\n\\n### Changelog\\n- \`webhook.ts\` — the dispatch failure line now logs at \`warn\` with its\\n  structured fields (\`evt\`, \`err\`, \`deliveryId\`) and the 500 unchanged.\\n- \`webhook.test.ts\` — the logging test expects the new level.\\n\\n### Notes\\n- OPS-77 asks to keep this line at \`error\`. We are deliberately going the\\n  other way: per ADR 0034 #5 a per-event page for a failure GitHub will\\n  redeliver is not operator-actionable, so it becomes \`warn\` and we alert\\n  on a sustained rate instead. Flagging the reversal here rather than\\n  silently leaving the ticket's instruction in place.\\n",
